<title>AUSTRALIA: Foxtel says has 200,000 subscribers.</title>
<headline>Foxtel says has 200,000 subscribers.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia's Foxtel pay television consortium said on Thursday that it had 200,000 subscribers, a rise of 50,000 in the past four months.</p>
<p>The company, which is equally owned by News Corp Ltd and the state-owned Telstra Corp, also said it had another 18,000 people waiting to become subscribers.</p>
<p>Foxtel is one of two major cable pay-tv groups in Australia.</p>
<p>The other major operator, Optus Vision, told Reuters that it had more than 180,000 subscribers but could not be more specific.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
